08/01/2026
- document the "encoding" option on OAuth2TargetPass, which controls how claim
  values are encoded into headers and environment variables; a claim value is
  UTF-8 but an HTTP header field value is US-ASCII, so a claim such as "Cem
  Özdemir" produced a header that strict clients reject. liboauth2 >= 2.3.1
  now defaults this to "latin1" (ISO-8859-1, anything that does not fit becomes
  "?"); "base64url" keeps the value intact and "none" restores the previous
  behaviour. NB: against liboauth2 2.3.0 and older the option is silently
  ignored, so the dependency wants raising to >= 2.3.1 at the next release
  thanks @maltesmann; closes #77
- return a 401 instead of a 500 when a token is rejected without an HTTP status
  code being set by liboauth2, which is the case for any locally detected JWT
  verification failure i.e. expiry, signature mismatch, "iss"/"aud"/"nbf"
  validation; the unset status code (0) was returned to Apache as OK, without a
  user being set, upon which Apache logs "AH00027: No authentication done but
  request not allowed without authentication" and returns a 500; only a 5xx is
  now relayed as-is, anything else results in a 401 with a WWW-Authenticate
  header; liboauth2 >= 2.3.1 sets the status code itself, this covers older
  versions as well
  thanks @smanolache; closes #94

